# Every text file is stored with LF and checked out with LF, on every platform.
# Without this, a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true rewrites files to
# CRLF on disk, and the contract tests under src/test/js read those files and
# match regular expressions containing a literal \n. Three of them failed for
# that reason alone while the content matched exactly.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch files are the exception; cmd.exe requires CRLF.
# These two rules come last so they win over the rule above.
/mvnw text eol=lf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
